{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/gate/utils/gate_macros.nim","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#354","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit","payload":"Pre-existing `make test` compilation blockers unrelated to debt remediation (out of Wave 1-4 scope). Primary defects: missing gate runner files src/gate/runners/architecture_config_gate.nim, src/gate/runners/context_size_guard.nim, src/gate/runners/debt_scan_gate.nim (referenced by macro but absent on disk); plus src/gate/utils/gate_macros.nim(102,30) invalid indentation and src/core/verified_axioms/ast_signature.nim not-all-cases-covered (IR API drift). Blocks local-ci[4/4] but NOT check-imports/check-arch/build. [REMEDIATED 2026-07-27: 3 missing gate runners created (architecture_config_gate.nim, context_size_guard.nim, debt_scan_gate.nim); gate_macros.nim:102 dead recordGateMetadata fragment removed (compile restored); ast_signature.nim drift resolved; bin/ax builds clean (EXIT=0)] [CLOSED 2026-07-28: All remediation phases completed] ","observedAt":" severity=high ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/core/observer/ast_builder.nim","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#355","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit","payload":"29 verification-critical `func` `except CatchableError: discard` silent swallows (residual of DEBT#275). These sit in effect-free core/verification funcs where silent discard is not a sanctioned best-effort; require manual error propagation (return Result/raise) rather than tagging. 12 files; see func_swallow_files list. [REMEDIATED 2026-07-27: all 12 files converted to AxiomError/Result[T,E] with explicit error propagation (no best-effort tagging on func core); topology_cli.nim + orchestrator.nim Result conversions applied] [CLOSED 2026-07-28: All remediation phases completed] ","observedAt":" severity=high ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/verification/certificates/","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#356","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit","payload":"68 Lean certificate .lean files in src/verification/certificates/ prove True by trivial (abbrev goal := True; theorem goal := by trivial). 34 base + 34 negative variants, all generated as LLM templates in feedback round 1. invariant is hardcoded True; strictSpecWarningRaised is true; implementationRefinesStepProvenSummary is false. [RESOLVED 2026-07-28: All 68 vacuous .lean files deleted. lean_vacuity_allowlist.json blanket exemption removed. Real proofs must be generated by the UAP pipeline with non-trivial invariants per Refinement Typed IR architecture (v5-planB).] ","observedAt":" severity=high ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/core/verifier/lean_repl_bridge.nim:46-69","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#357","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-29","payload":"runVerificationPipeline*() returns true after calling handleZ3BmcResult(...) regardless of Z3 result. Z3 verification failure is silently ignored and the pipeline reports success. Found in both src/core/verifier/lean_repl_bridge.nim:46-69 and src/verification/lean_repl_bridge.nim:346-358. ","observedAt":" severity=high ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/verification/certificate_manager.nim:30-46","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#358","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-29","payload":"validateCertGreenWritable*(node: JsonNode) returns true when the node is not a JSON object, even though comments say green certificates must have non-empty winning strategy. Also, FunctionCertificate validation returns true for non-certGreen/non-certVerifiedAxiom statuses without checking actual certificate content. ","observedAt":" severity=high ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"tools/hermetic_build.nim:1119-1135","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#359","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-29","payload":"verifyInvariantHash() returns true if either architecture_invariants.nim or expected hash file is missing, after only logging a warning. checkManifestStaleness() also returns true if manifest/ gate directory is missing. These are warning-only checks that never fail the build. ","observedAt":" severity=medium ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/gate/pipeline_orchestrator.nim:256-258","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#360","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-29","payload":"Cache lookup errors are ignored with discard (pipeline_orchestrator.nim:256-258). When a gate entry cannot be resolved, gatePassed is set to true with comment 'Can't resolve → pass-through' (pipeline_orchestrator.nim:285-300). This allows unresolvable gates to silently pass. ","observedAt":" severity=high ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/infrastructure/gate_signing/axiom_prove.nim:128-133","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#361","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-29","payload":"trivialProof() returns an SMT environment that is 'trivially satisfiable' when no .smt2 files exist. The generated SMT has no meaningful constraints but is presented as a proof artifact. This is a trivially-SAT SMT query matching theater signature #4. ","observedAt":" severity=high ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/core/proof/proof_vacuity_gate.nim:242-250","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#362","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-29","payload":"verifyNonTrivialityWithFallback returns (true, false, '') when no security constraints exist, and (true, true, 'z3_timeout_or_error') on Z3 timeout/error. This fallback-to-trivial path allows vacuous proofs to pass. Also, sourceHasAxiomPurePragma can mute vacuity warnings via pragma exemption. ","observedAt":" severity=high ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/cli/payload_bridge.nim:16-28","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#363","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-29","payload":"Filters out '(assert true)' and returns empty SMT payload if no constraints remain. This is a direct anti-vacuity bypass path: the system removes the thing it should be checking before proof generation. ","observedAt":" severity=medium ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/gate/manifest.d/auto-heal.json:1-0","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#365","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-29","payload":"Manifest entries were updated from missing bin/ executables to Nim source paths so gate resolver/CAS can compile the real runner on demand. REMEDIATED 2026-07-29: added missing main entry points where needed, updated gate_registry.nim to accept source-path entries, and refreshed manifest entries for auto-heal, binary-artifact, core-invariant, delegation, doc-completeness, external-cli-smoke, gateway-test, intent, language-ban, nim-check, policy-validator, spec-binding, spec-presence, test-coverage, and verification-auditor. ","observedAt":" severity=high ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
