{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/verification/lean_lsp_protocol.nim:287-298","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#369","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-30","payload":"Bare except: discard at lean_lsp_protocol.nim:295-296 silently swallows uncategorizable exceptions during LSP process liveness check. While CatchableError returns an error response, the catch-all discard means system-level failures (e.g., OS-level handle errors on peekExitCode) are ignored — violating AGENTS.md §0.9 Theater Signature #2. The post-hover liveness check claims to verify LSP process health but provides no evidence when unexpected errors occur. [FIXED 2026-07-30: replaced discard with stderr logging + error response] ","observedAt":" severity=medium ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/personas/scribe.nim:52-54","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#370","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-30_parallel","payload":"When synthesizeLeanTheorem*() encounters ANY exception (network failure, JSON parse error, subprocess crash), it returns ok(emptyArtifact) with verified=false. The caller sees apparent success with no theorem, no tactic trace. This breaks the entire Scribe→Judge handoff chain by converting all failures into pass-through behavior. [NEW 2026-07-30 from parallel subagent audit of src/personas/] ","observedAt":" severity=critical ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/personas/legislator.nim:244","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#372","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-30_parallel","payload":"In queryViaStdioPipe*(), process cleanup in finally block silently discards exceptions without # axiom:best-effort(ioboundary catch) tag. Violates codebase-wide tagging convention. While impact is low (cleanup code), it sets bad precedent. [NEW 2026-07-30 from parallel subagent audit of src/personas/] ","observedAt":" severity=low ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"tools/verify_lfs_integrity.nim:8-34","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#373","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-30_parallel","payload":"verifyLfsIntegrity*() emits warning when vendor/z3/lib/libz3.so is missing but continues to return true at line 33. A repo where Z3 was never fetched passes LFS integrity verification. Function name promises integrity verification but allows critical artifact absence to pass silently. [NEW 2026-07-30 from parallel subagent audit of tools/] ","observedAt":" severity=medium ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"tools/hooks/semantic_grounding_hook.nim:43,61,118-121","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#374","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-30_parallel","payload":"Main proc wraps everything in try/except that prints error to stderr then ALWAYS calls quit(0). If hook crashes due to invalid JSON, bad project root, or any error, it exits with status 0 (success). Downstream CI/gate systems relying on exit code get false confidence. No structured audit trail. [NEW 2026-07-30 from parallel subagent audit of tools/] ","observedAt":" severity=high ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/verification/state_manager.nim:495","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#375","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-30_parallel","payload":"saveProofState*() calls atomicWriteText(path, renderJsonMultiline(state)) but discards its Result[bool, string] return value via discard. If atomicWriteText fails, failure is silently swallowed and proc falls through to ok(true). Proof state persistence failures are reported as success. Critical trust boundary violation. [NEW 2026-07-30 from parallel subagent audit of src/verification/] ","observedAt":" severity=high ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/verification/pipeline_negative_scan_part2.nim:356-364","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#376","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-30_parallel","payload":"When execCmdWithTimeout('z3 -smt2 ...') raises (Z3 unavailable, crash), except handler falls through to buildCounterExampleJson with status='fallback'. Produces JSON artifact that looks like genuine counterexample but was never computed by Z3. Downstream consumers see solver:'z3', status:'fallback' and may treat fabricated evidence as real. [NEW 2026-07-30 from parallel subagent audit of src/verification/] ","observedAt":" severity=high ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/core/session/session_parser_validators.nim:62-64","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#377","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-30_parallel","payload":"isAnyString*(s: string): bool discards its input parameter entirely and unconditionally returns true. Function claims to validate that string is 'any string' but performs zero validation. Matches theater signature #1 exactly: return true without evaluating condition it claims to check. [NEW 2026-07-30 from parallel subagent audit of src/core/] ","observedAt":" severity=medium ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/core/observer/scanner.nim:70-71","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#378","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-30_parallel","payload":"Entire walkDirRec loop's exceptions are swallowed silently at lines 70-71 with no logging, no error propagation, no record. If directory walking fails (permissions, broken symlinks), scan produces incomplete result with no indication. Unlike inner catches that add to result.errors, outer catch drops entire walk silently. [NEW 2026-07-30 from parallel subagent audit of src/core/] ","observedAt":" severity=medium ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/core/observer/scanner.nim:123,151,159","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#379","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-30_parallel","payload":"Three locations use bare except: discard when writing to stderr (lines 123, 151, 159). Violates project's own exception_guard.nim policy that bans bare except: clauses. While intent is best-effort logging, bare except catches system-level errors (file descriptor exhaustion, OOM kills) that should arguably propagate. [NEW 2026-07-30 from parallel subagent audit of src/core/] ","observedAt":" severity=low-medium ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/gate/runners/effect_inference_gate.nim:116-121","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#380","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-30_parallel","payload":"When severity is 'warn' (default per getAxiomEnv(evGateSeverity, 'warn')), gate reports violations but still returns ok:true. Under default configuration, gate always passes regardless of how many I/O procs are found missing {.axiomEffect: IOEffect.} annotations. Gate claims to enforce effect annotation policy but guarantees nothing under default settings. [NEW 2026-07-30 from parallel subagent audit of src/gate/] ","observedAt":" severity=high ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/gate/runners/documentation_first_gate.nim:433-436,629-632","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#381","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-30_parallel","payload":"When trigger config contains zero triggers (misconfiguration, missing config, parse failure), gate passes with only WARN-level message and quit(0). Gate's verification condition is vacuously true because there are no conditions to verify. Misconfigured gate should fail closed, not pass open. VFS variant at lines 629-632 has identical pattern. [NEW 2026-07-30 from parallel subagent audit of src/gate/] ","observedAt":" severity=medium ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/core/ir/ir_to_lean.nim","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#384","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-31_parallel_full","payload":"irToLeanRefinedDefinition generates f(args) = f(args) tautologies when no postcondition exists, with tactic 'first ","observedAt":" (simp [*]; done) ","toolchainContext":" sorry'. generateOptimalTactic falls back to 'sorry -- Escalated to Z3 SMT BMC'. encodeLeanTheoremFromIr converts these to SMT queries that are trivially UNSAT. This produces 'verified' output that constrains nothing. The correct pattern exists in src/core/trusted/ir_to_lean.nim:545-546 which skips generation when postConditions.len == 0. [NEW 2026-07-31 from parallel full-codebase theater audit] "}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"AGENTS.md","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#385","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-07-31_parallel_full","payload":"AGENTS.md §1 states 'AXIOM_BYPASS_GATES 환경변수 완전 제거' but src/gate/runners/language_ban_gate.nim:163,209 prints bypass instructions using AXIOM_BYPASS_GATES=1. Also docs/spec/hooks_architecture.md and docs/spec/break_glass_protocol.md describe the bypass as active. The claim of complete removal is false. [NEW 2026-07-31 from parallel full-codebase theater audit] ","observedAt":" severity=high ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
