{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"tools/ci/ci_health_checker.nim","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#393","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"quirk_audit","payload":"JsonNode.getOrDefault(key) returns nil when key absent (no default param). Accessing .kind on the result SIGSEGVs. Guard with isNil check or hasKey before .kind access. Fixed in tools/ci/ci_health_checker.nim parseCircleCiPipelines; 877 usage sites project-wide, most chain .getStr()/.getInt() which are nil-safe. See docs/spec/nim_json_getordefault_quirk.md. ","observedAt":" severity=low ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":".circleci/config.yml","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#394","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit","payload":"CI job verify-coverage-guard (.circleci/config.yml) restores only nim-deps-v1-* caches, never coverage-baseline-v1-*. coverage_guard.nim baseline resolution: git fetch (fails on shallow clone) -> data/.coverage_baseline_main.json (missing without restore) -> First Run Safe at coverage_guard.nim:205-213 saves current coverage as baseline and returns 0 unconditionally. Also save_cache key uses {{ epoch }} which changes hourly, making restore impossible even if added. Gate has appearance of regression protection but passes every clean CI run. ","observedAt":" severity=high ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"Makefile","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#395","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-08-02_parallel_full","payload":"Makefile targets check-nim-theater (tools/ci/check_nim_theater.nim), check-lean-vacuity (tools/ci/check_lean_vacuity.nim), check-vacuity, check-vacuity-simple exist but NOT invoked by .circleci/continue.yml verify-static (runs only env-check/check-imports/check-mcp/check-debt/verify-all) nor by make verify-all (only meta_spec_gate). Pre-commit/pre-push hooks run only anti_theater_gate. The dedicated theater-pattern and Lean-vacuity scanners protect nothing automatically — theater introduced into src/tests/proofs would pass CI undetected. The mutation_harness validates static_gate_scanner.nim only, not these Φ2 scanners. Only theater check wired into CI is the pre-commit anti_theater_gate (git-diff added-lines only). ","observedAt":" severity=high ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/core/audit/theater_linter.nim","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#396","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-08-02_parallel_full","payload":"src/core/audit/theater_linter.nim defines scanTheaterSource (real detection logic) and macOS lintTheaterPatterns macro, but the macro is never imported/called in any src/ module, not wired into config.nims, Makefile, or CI. Referenced only in tests and docs/spec/theater_linter.md. It CLAIMS to provide compile-time theater-pattern detection (§0.9) but enforces nothing because no build path invokes it. NOTE: the separately-wired check_nim_theater.nim is a different tool; this specific compile-time macro is dead. ","observedAt":" severity=medium ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"proofs/GateInvariants/CacheKeyCompleteness.lean","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#398","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-08-02_parallel_full","payload":"CacheKeyCompleteness.lean:47 declares 'axiom hash_injective : ∀ a b, computeKey a = computeKey b → a = b' and derives cache_key_complete / cache_key_complete_explicit by one-line deduction from this axiom. This is circular: it asserts the very injectivity/collision-resistance that the cache-key-uniqueness theorems are meant to prove. SHA-256 collision resistance is 'believed' not proven. Presents an assumption as a verification guarantee. Additionally the Lean proof layer (lake build) is not compiled in CI, and the axiomatization would go undetected since check_lean_vacuity scans for sorry/hasSorry but not axiom declarations. ","observedAt":" severity=medium ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"tests/gateway/json_utils_feature_test.nim","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#399","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"theater_audit_2026-08-02_parallel_full","payload":"tests/gateway/json_utils_feature_test.nim contains 3 tests each ending in 'doAssert false, \"ASSERTION NOT IMPLEMENTED...\"' (lines 22, 35, 48) — 100% stub density per §0.8. Auto-generated by tools/scaffold_feature_test.nim:325,342 which emits doAssert false placeholders. Claims (via suite name) to cover json_utils.feature scenarios but always-fails asserting nothing real. Systemic source: the scaffold generator emits disguised stubs that become committed test files. ","observedAt":" severity=medium ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
