{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/verification/batch_uap/loop_depth_scheduler.nim","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#415","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"prove_crash_investigation_2026-08-04","payload":"bin/ax prove with AXIOM_PROVE_WORKERS>1 crashes with SIGSEGV (Illegal storage access, nil read) immediately after 'deterministic-scheduler: depth=0 items=4890'. Two compounding defects in src/verification/batch_uap/loop_depth_scheduler.nim: (1) limit check at lines 344-346 compares report.nodeReports.len (never grows during the filter loop, primed not subtracted) so pendingItems accumulates all 4890 depth-0 items instead of the --limit batch; (2) fingerprint/node workers spawned via malebolgia receive SorterState, Table[string,string], and a shared ptr ParallelNodeContext — main-thread heap objects dereferenced on worker threads under --mm:arc --threads:on, violating section 0.6a (value-type only across spawn). {.cast(gcsafe).} at line 278 suppresses the Nim 2.2 isolation check that would have caught this. Serial path (workers=1) is unaffected and is now the CI default. ","observedAt":" severity=high ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
