{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":".gitignore","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#414","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"determinism_audit_2026-08-03","payload":"persistVsrLedger (axiom_engine.nim:158-161) appends timestamped records via fmAppend on every `ax prove` execution, causing file changes that trigger git status modifications. This violates determinism (§0.2) since identical commands produce different file hashes. The file was tracked via .gitignore exception '!logs/audit/'. Added logs/audit/vsr_ledger.jsonl to .gitignore (after unignore patterns) and git rm --cached to untrack while preserving local file. ","observedAt":" severity=medium ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"src/verification/batch_uap/loop_depth_scheduler.nim","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#415","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"prove_crash_investigation_2026-08-04","payload":"bin/ax prove with AXIOM_PROVE_WORKERS>1 crashes with SIGSEGV (Illegal storage access, nil read) immediately after 'deterministic-scheduler: depth=0 items=4890'. Two compounding defects in src/verification/batch_uap/loop_depth_scheduler.nim: (1) limit check at lines 344-346 compares report.nodeReports.len (never grows during the filter loop, primed not subtracted) so pendingItems accumulates all 4890 depth-0 items instead of the --limit batch; (2) fingerprint/node workers spawned via malebolgia receive SorterState, Table[string,string], and a shared ptr ParallelNodeContext — main-thread heap objects dereferenced on worker threads under --mm:arc --threads:on, violating section 0.6a (value-type only across spawn). {.cast(gcsafe).} at line 278 suppresses the Nim 2.2 isolation check that would have caught this. Serial path (workers=1) is unaffected and is now the CI default. ","observedAt":" severity=high ","toolchainContext":" status=closed"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"data/verification_scope.lock","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#416","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"Tier 4 classification 2026-08-10","payload":"CHC routing fix applied: loopSimpleFor unary relaxation, CHC-First routing, BMC fallback split. This enables CHC/Spacer inductive loop proving for previously unverified functions. Expected VKD improvement: from 5/40 (0.125) to 18~25/40 (0.45~0.625). Action plan: run `ax prove` to verify which functions now pass CHC, then update the count. Remaining unverified: the axiomOpaque-marked functions (firstArrayField, toStringList, normalizedResources, normalizedMutations) plus any that fail CHC proving. ","observedAt":" severity=medium ","toolchainContext":" status=open"}
{"kind":"okSourceMarker","subject":"config.nims","semanticIdentity":"DEBT#417","snapshotId":"79da0df33c109a6c433fa56aedd75aebc2fe0f64","source":"architecture_debt_audit","payload":".git/index는 VCS staging state이며 compiler semantic state가 아님. 로컬 dirty-marker로 envHash 포함. 이상은 cache identity = toolchain/config/source/dependency. config.nims 불가침 제약으로 지금 수정 않음. ","observedAt":" severity=medium ","toolchainContext":" status=open"}
